  "about": "The Steam bridge's allow-list (docs/steam-bridge.md, phase 3), reviewed by hand. A method not listed is refused. mode: call (a round trip; the broker checks as listed), hand (written in bridge_local.c: answered in the game, from the snapshot or fixed), refuse. strings: an input string's longest length in bytes. buffers: an output buffer, the parameter that holds its size and the most the broker accepts. outs: pointers the method writes one value through. ownLobby: CSteamID parameters that must be a lobby the game made this session. range: [min, max] for an integer parameter. printable: strings that may hold only printable ASCII. logged: strings the broker writes to its log on every call.",
